        "text": "On en parlait il y a quelques temps <@U6FGQ47L7> !\nCa commence déjà à ‘bouger’, mais plus un effet d’annonce à mon sens, de la part de la startup *Neurable*\n\nIntéressant l’illustration avec les LEDs au dos de l’appareil pour le feedback\nPing <@U03HY4P8V> <@U04T6ATLX> <@U0KKC7AQ6> \n\n“With the Neurable SDK, Unity developers can easily integrate brain-activity as a control input into any game.\nBrain signal acquisition is accomplished through our upgraded headband for the HTC Vive. Simply remove the elastic straps in the back and replace them with our straps. Our solution is a demonstration prototype of how brain sensors and neurotechnology can be integrated with AR\/VR devices.”\n\n<https:\/\/medium.com\/neurable\/announcing-the-worlds-first-brain-computer-interface-for-virtual-reality-a3110db62607>\n\nLe SDK Kit sort en beta limitée\n<http:\/\/www.neurable.com\/developers>",
